## 1. `PHASE-00` Readiness Items (`[EXECUTE]` vs `[INFO_NOTE]`, `IP5`, `IP9`)

Every plan begins with `PHASE-00` so `code_writer` never stalls mid-phase waiting for environments, fixtures, migrations, or credentials. Tag each item explicitly:
- **`[EXECUTE]`**: A deterministic command or setup step executed and verified (`PASS` / `FAIL`) before `PHASE-01` begins.
- **`[INFO_NOTE]`**: Verified reference context (existing test accounts, environment URLs, pinned flags) recorded for downstream phases.

