## 3. Definition of Done (DoD) per Phase (`IP6`, `IP7`, `IP17`)

A behavior phase (`PHASE-NN`) is complete and ready for phase commit checkpoint (`IP7`) only when every item below is satisfied:

- [ ] Every task check command in `PHASE-NN` exited `0` (`PASS`) on the current revision.
- [ ] Workspace analyzer / linter / type-checker (`{{analyzer_cmd}}`) exited `0` (`PASS`) with zero new warnings or errors.
- [ ] Unit and integration tests covering agreed pass/fail cases and `## Review focus` edge cases owned by `PHASE-NN` are implemented in this phase and report `PASS` (`IP11`, `IP17`).
- [ ] Documentation updates required by `PHASE-NN` behavior are completed inside this phase (`IP17`).
{{extra_dod_items}}
- [ ] Phase handoff evidence records exact commands run, working directories, git revision, and `PASS` results (`NOT_RUN`, `BLOCKED`, and `UNVERIFIED` never count as `PASS`).
- [ ] Only after phase checks and review acceptance pass, create the verified phase/sub-ticket commit checkpoint per `IP7` (`G3`, `M10`).

